        "id": 99086,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-04-03T15:45:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>How did Fixed Point kill you in that instance? If it was still out when Devious Disruption entered play (which I gather from context is what happened), it wouldn't matter what you did - no-one would be dying right there and then <span class=\"bbcode-i\">because</span> of Fixed Point. If you'd not destroyed any of your stuff (or even if you had) and the resultant damage took you into negative hp, then you'd be in negative hp. If you were still there when Fixed Point went away, <span class=\"bbcode-i\">then</span> you'd be incapped. But until that point, you'd've had the rest of the round in which to nuke Blade before Fixed Point went away at the start of the environment turn.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:26:57.006Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
